<title>SINGAPORE: INDIA BUYS ONE KERO CARGO FROM MOBIL IN SEP TENDER.</title>
<headline>INDIA BUYS ONE KERO CARGO FROM MOBIL IN SEP TENDER.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has awarded one cargo of superior kerosene to Mobil in its September tender, traders said on Monday.</p>
<p>The cargo was awarded at seven cents per barrel over Singapore spot quotes on a cost-and-freight (c-and-f) basis to the Indian ports of Madras or Haldia on the east coast, they said.</p>
<p>The tender sought 40,000-45,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>In its tender for August deliveries, IOC also purchased one 40,000-45,000 tonne cargo from Mobil, at three cents over spot Singapore quotes on a c-and-f basis.  </p>
